{
  "series_title": "Dragon Ball Super",
  "research_status": "COMPLETE — all 131 episodes of Dragon Ball Super classified canon/filler/mixed. The 14-episode filler list (4, 15, 42-46, 68-70, 73-76) is corroborated by three independently-fetched sources (ListFist, ComicBook.com, The Mary Sue) that agree exactly. A fourth guide (animefillerguide.com) was checked and discarded — it listed a substantially different, larger filler set (including episodes 16-17, 52, and 87-90, none of which appear in any of the three agreeing sources' lists), so it was treated as unreliable rather than a genuine data point, the same call made about aniyume.net's contradictory Fullmetal Alchemist: Brotherhood list earlier in this same research pass. Episodes 1-2 are recorded as mixed per ListFist (partial filler alongside real story content); episode 89 is also mixed per ListFist but flagged in its own status_note as the one call backed by only a single source. Dragon Ball Super's unusual production history (much of its story originates from Toriyama's own movie scripts and outlines adapted into anime before or alongside Toyotaro's manga, rather than the more typical anime-trails-manga pattern) means the canon/filler line here is fan-consensus-driven rather than a strict manga-publication-order check — consistent with how this project's other shows are compiled, but worth flagging given how different this show's production actually was. No episode titles included — left for the existing backfill_episode_titles_from_anilist.py (#73) pass, same as Dragon Ball Z. Complete, gap-free, non-overlapping coverage of 1-131 confirmed before writing this file.",
